overview.problemStatement:
Let x, y : ℝ → ℝ be C¹ and 2π-periodic, and let φ : ℝ → ℝ be C¹ with φ(2π) = φ(0) + 2π (it commutes with the period). Then:
- (arc length, assuming φ' ≥ 0)  ∫₀²π √((x∘φ)'² + (y∘φ)'²) = ∫₀²π √(x'² + y'²);
- (signed area)  ∫₀²π ((x∘φ)·(y∘φ)' − (y∘φ)·(x∘φ)') = ∫₀²π (x·y' − y·x').
